# Moves a folder and every file in it that isn't in the trash: all of them,
# or none. Files in the trash keep their paths. Moving a folder that is already at `new path` succeeds, so a retry
# whose answer was lost is safe.
METHOD move (path: TEXT) to (new path: TEXT)
    RETURNS (files: LIST files/file summary)
    ERRORS [
        # No file is in this folder.
        no such folder,
        # Nothing moved.
        (paths: LIST: TEXT) taken by other files,
        # Nothing moved.
        (path: TEXT) would be both file and folder,
    ] + paths/bad path,
